---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Company — CFLabs"
  description="CFLabs builds computational infrastructure for AI and blockchain, backed by Intchains Group in silicon and Aoraki Labs in AI. Partners, focus and how to reach us."
  section="company"
>
  <section class="wrap section--tight">
    <p class="eyebrow">Company</p>
    <h1 style="margin-top:12px;font-size:clamp(30px,5vw,50px)">
      A small team that keeps<br />picking expensive workloads.
    </h1>
    <p class="lede" style="margin-top:16px">
      CFLabs builds computational infrastructure for AI and blockchain. Our people come
      from semiconductors, cryptography and machine learning, and the thread through every
      project has been the same: take a workload that costs too much to be useful, and
      move the cost.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section rule-top">
    <p class="eyebrow">Backing</p>
    <h2 style="margin-top:10px">Two houses behind the work.</h2>
    <div class="grid grid--2" style="margin-top:28px">
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Intchains Group</h3>
        <p class="muted">
          A leading provider of integrated solutions built on high-performance
          application-specific integrated circuits, with the ancillary hardware and
          software around them. Intchains is where the silicon and the supply chain
          come from.
        </p>
        <p><a href="https://intchains.com/" rel="noopener">intchains.com ↗</a></p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Aoraki Labs</h3>
        <p class="muted">
          "We build the next generation of computational infrastructure for AI and
          blockchain." Aoraki Labs is the AI side of the house — video generation
          research, the Phosor platform, and the open research index behind both.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="https://aoraki-labs.io/" rel="noopener">aoraki-labs.io ↗</a>
          <span class="muted"> · </span>
          <a href="https://github.com/aoraki-labs-ai" rel="noopener">github ↗</a>
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section rule-top">
    <p class="eyebrow">Technology partners</p>
    <div class="logos" style="margin-top:20px">
      <img src="/img/logo_intchains.png" alt="Intchains Group" width="546" height="111" loading="lazy" />
      <img src="/img/logo_risczero.png" alt="RISC Zero" width="546" height="111" loading="lazy" />
      <img src="/img/logo_succinct.png" alt="Succinct" width="546" height="111" loading="lazy" />
    </div>
    <p class="tnote" style="margin-top:20px">
      Our proof-system work has been built around RISC Zero and Succinct's zkVMs, and our
      hardware work with Intchains. Details are in the
      <a href="/research/#zk">research papers</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section rule-top">
    <p class="eyebrow">Open work</p>
    <h2 style="margin-top:10px">Some of it is public.</h2>
    <div class="grid grid--2" style="margin-top:26px">
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Awesome Video AI Research</h3>
        <p class="muted">
          A curated index of video AI — architectures, models, datasets, inference
          optimisation and post-training — with the primary papers linked, plus our own
          working notes on the gap between open and closed models.
        </p>
        <p><a href="https://github.com/aoraki-labs-ai/Awesome-Video-AI-Research" rel="noopener">On GitHub ↗</a></p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Agent Trust Stack</h3>
        <p class="muted">
          A continuously updated, source-linked report on trustworthy privacy and
          verifiable AI for the agent era. Every checkable number is a record carrying its
          source, its confidence tier and the observation that would overturn it — a number
          without a source fails the build.
        </p>
        <p><a href="https://github.com/aoraki-labs-ai/agent-trust-stack" rel="noopener">On GitHub ↗</a></p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section rule-top">
    <div class="contact">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Contact</p>
        <h2 style="margin-top:10px">Talk to us.</h2>
        <p class="lede" style="margin-top:10px">
          Video generation at volume, a custom model, or acceleration work on a proving
          system — one email gets to the people who would do it.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="contact__links">
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href="mailto:hello@cflabs.ai">hello@cflabs.ai</a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="https://x.com/CFrontier_Labs" rel="noopener">@CFrontier_Labs ↗</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>

  .contact {
    display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 26px; flex-wrap: wrap;
    border: 1px solid var(--line); border-left: 3px solid var(--mint);
    border-radius: var(--radius); background: var(--surface); padding: 30px 32px;
  }
  .contact__links { display: flex; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
</style>
